v 3
d gepwreg. Percentile Weights Regression with analytical standard errors
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar
d Universite Laval and Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP)
d Support: aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260916
d
d Description:
d gepwreg estimates the Percentile Weights Regression (PWR) of Araar
d (2016, 2023): the local marginal effect of the regressors on the outcome
d for observations whose rank in the distribution of the outcome (or of
d another ranking variable) is in the neighbourhood of a target percentile.
d Version 1.4 (factor-variable fix) implements the results of Araar (2026,
d doi:10.5281/zenodo.20315684): closed-form analytical standard errors by
d linearisation, which account for the estimation of the kernel weights;
d an MSE-optimal bandwidth chosen by a two-step plug-in rule; Taylor
d linearisation under a complex survey design declared by svyset; a pairs
d bootstrap that re-estimates the weights at each replication; and ranking
d on any variable other than the outcome.  gepwreg_setable, a post-
d estimation command, compares the standard errors; a dialog box is included.
d
d bkf98I.dta, retrieved by net get, is the Burkina Faso 1998 household
d survey extract used in the paper and in the help file examples.
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
f gepwreg.ado
f gepwreg_setable.ado
f gepwreg.sthlp
f gepwreg.dlg
f bkf98I.dta
